// TEST: Unannotated Scalar Param Broadcast Return
// The positive half of 033's pair, and the reason 033 is a rejection of the
// CALL and not of the declaration.
//
// `f` is character-for-character the function 033 rejects a call to. Its
// parameter `x` is unannotated and nothing closes it, so it defaults to a
// scalar; the declared array return is then filled by BROADCASTING the
// scalar body into every slot. That is well-defined, it is what codegen
// emits, and it is what a scalar argument gets. A rank rule at the
// application seam has to leave this alone — which is exactly why the
// declared array return must not be read as forcing `x` to be an array.
function f(x, s: Float) -> Array<Float like Idx<4>> =
    x * s

let r = f(3.0, 2.0)
// EXPECT: r = [6, 6, 6, 6]
